      "conclusion": "313/543 reference values coincide EXACTLY with an experimental value somewhere in the same file (z=+22.8 vs a grid null of 105.9 +- 9.1), and every value is on the 0.1 kcal/mol grid, so the reference channel draws from the same literature value pool as the experimental column. It nevertheless shares a value with the specific row's own experimental value only ONCE (1/543) and never (0/543) with the experimental value of the same fragment pair in another molecule, so it is a INDEPENDENT DRAW from that literature pool, not a copy of the benchmark answer. This is what makes it usable as an independent probe of reference-value heterogeneity, and it is also why its error (MAE 5.486) is large.",
